`allow.write_paths` contains `~/x`. A home-relative path is outside the workspace, and SPEC §5.2 condition 3 says an escaping allow path refuses the whole manifest. Refused in the schema without lookahead (`^~`), so a Go or Rust validator loads the rule; the registry re-checks the resolved path as well. A `deny.paths` entry MAY be home-relative, because refusing to touch `~/.ssh` is meaningful even though no allow could grant it.
